Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for PaperPilot

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency and its 74 sub-packages

### 2. Modified frontend/src/App.tsx
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main app div (after the AddDocumentModal)
- The Analytics component is now included in the signed-in state, ensuring analytics tracking for authenticated users

## Implementation Details:

Following the React/Vite-specific instructions from the official documentation, the Analytics component was integrated into the main App component. This placement ensures analytics tracking across all user interactions within the application.

The component is lightweight and will automatically:
- Track page views
- Collect Web Vitals metrics
- Send analytics data to Vercel when the app is deployed

## Verification:

✅ TypeScript type checking passed (npm run typecheck)
✅ Production build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No errors or warnings introduced
✅ All dependencies properly installed

## Next Steps:

After deployment to Vercel, analytics will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab. The analytics script will automatically collect:
- Page views and user navigation
- Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
- Custom events (if configured in the future)

To verify the integration after deployment, check the browser's Network tab for requests to the Vercel analytics endpoint.
